# Keep the build context to what
# `cargo build --release --locked -p myrlet-hub -p myrlet-worker-daemon -p myrlet-cli`
# needs — `Cargo.toml`, `Cargo.lock`, `crates/`, and `apps/` — plus `docker/` for
# the all-in-one entrypoint. `apps/web/` stays included: the `web-builder` stage
# compiles the built-in UI from source.

# Build output and toolchain state
target/
**/target/

# Web UI build state: `apps/web/` sources and `docker/` stay in the context, but a
# stale local `node_modules/` or `dist/` must never leak into the image. The
# `web-builder` stage installs its own dependencies and rebuilds `dist/`.
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/

# VCS metadata and CI configuration
.git/
.github/

# Docs and brand assets are never compiled into the binaries
docs/
assets/
*.md
**/*.md

# OS clutter
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
